    "detailed_description": "A girl suffering from hallucinations tries her best to live a normal life in the megapolis. She sees an advertisement for a certain doctor presenting a revolutionary technology for diagnosing and treating the psyche, &quot;G.L.A.Z.A&quot;.<br><br>The heroine hesitates a little and decides to take a chance to dig into her problems and get rid of the need to drink pills. Advertising turns out to be truthful, but first she needs to go through a thorough analysis. And she herself has to dive into the wicked mind and understand the cause of all the problems. <br><br>Darkness, monsters, ghosts of the past and a cheerful girl-guide will help the main character along the way, but only to an extent, so that he understands the depth of her own despair.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Features</h2><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>6 endings<br></li><li>6 dozens of minutes of confusing plot<br></li><li>6 definitions of why you can't talk to the dead</li></ul>",
